ep 'ADR 0037' hits: tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_dc_force_reindex.py:4 'UNBOUNDED background-reindex latency (ADR 0037 §3)'; tests/external/live_jira_dc/_dc_support.py:283 'UNBOUNDED (ADR 0037 §3): ... the reindex thread'; tests/external/live_jira_dc/conftest.py:9 'eventual-consistency discipline (ADR 0037 §3)'","docs/adr/0085-reconciler-live-validation-harness.md:3 'previously ADR 0037 ... reassigned to 0085'; line 58 heading '### 3. Eventual-consistency discipline'; line 60 'search index lags both a create and a delete by an **unbounded** interval'","docs/adr/0055 has zero 'unbounded' matches and zero '§3'; line 282 'Search-index lag' row is about 'keyless-pending recovery ... creates a duplicate issue', not unbounded reindex","f449 description text: 'background reindex is UNBOUNDED (ADR 0037 s3)'"],"finding":"The plan's chosen replacement citation target (ADR 0055 / the 'Search-index lag' row) appears to be the wrong ADR for f449's 'ADR 0037 s3' unbounded-reindex support. The repo's other 'ADR 0037 §3' citations for the unbounded background reindex (tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_dc_force_reindex.py:4, tests/external/live_jira_dc/_dc_support.py:283, tests/external/live_jira_dc/conftest.py:9/276) map to ADR 0085 (docs/adr/0085-reconciler-live-validation-harness.md), which docs/adr/RENUMBERING.md and the ADR header show was renumbered from the earliest-landed old ADR 0037 by story 0743. ADR 0085 line 60 states 'Jira's search index lags both a create and a delete by an **unbounded** interval' under the literal '### 3. Eventual-consistency discipline' heading — matching both the 'unbounded' semantics and the '§3'/'s3' section token in f449's description. ADR 0055 contains no 'unbounded' string and no '§3'; its line-282 'Search-index lag' row is a one-line table entry about keyless-pending recovery creating a duplicate issue, not the unbounded-reindex characterization f449 cites.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb16e2f1c030bb2c9","impact":1.0,"is_pr